1
00:00:00,251 --> 00:00:01,377
Thank you.

2
00:00:01,460 --> 00:00:04,422
You're the only person
who made this occasion special for me.

3
00:00:05,089 --> 00:00:06,716
You were threatened and scared.

4
00:00:06,799 --> 00:00:08,801
I can't leave you. I'll protect you.

5
00:00:09,927 --> 00:00:10,928
Someone is scaring me!

6
00:00:11,637 --> 00:00:12,805
The entire campaign is canceled.

7
00:00:12,888 --> 00:00:18,853
But we shouldn't stop looking
for whoever leaked the campaign.

8
00:00:19,228 --> 00:00:21,814
You want to eliminate the person
who's protecting me

9
00:00:21,897 --> 00:00:22,982
from everything.

10
00:00:23,566 --> 00:00:26,318
That trust is making you soft…
Ms. Diana Aragon.

11
00:00:26,402 --> 00:00:28,487
I've got Diana wrapped around my finger.

12
00:00:28,571 --> 00:00:30,740
She falls in love with me

13
00:00:30,823 --> 00:00:32,408
and she won't be able to escape.

14
00:00:41,584 --> 00:00:43,586
-Teddy.
-What are you doing here?

15
00:00:43,669 --> 00:00:44,795
I just want to ask you something.

16
00:00:44,879 --> 00:00:47,131
What makes you think
I'd cooperate with you?

17
00:00:48,924 --> 00:00:49,967
No.

18
00:00:51,260 --> 00:00:53,387
I didn't talk to that reporter.

19
00:00:53,846 --> 00:00:55,222
I didn't answer his questions.

20
00:00:55,306 --> 00:00:58,642
Why would I give information
that could hurt my own family?

21
00:00:58,976 --> 00:01:01,145
We have another piece of evidence
against you.

22
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:08,611
You are suspended effective immediately

23
00:01:08,694 --> 00:01:11,655
for leaking confidential information

24
00:01:11,739 --> 00:01:12,948
to a rival company.

25
00:01:17,244 --> 00:01:18,287
I want to talk to my sister.

26
00:01:18,788 --> 00:01:19,955
This is a setup.

27
00:01:20,581 --> 00:01:23,667
You will be summoned
for an administrator hearing

28
00:01:23,751 --> 00:01:25,044
-so you can defend yourself.
-You!

29
00:01:25,127 --> 00:01:27,797
-Let go of me!
-Sir, calm down!

30
00:01:29,173 --> 00:01:30,966
I know you're behind all of this!

31
00:01:31,050 --> 00:01:33,594
You set me up! You'll pay for this!

32
00:01:33,677 --> 00:01:35,179
Just you wait!

33
00:01:35,262 --> 00:01:36,305
Let me go! Hey!

34
00:01:36,806 --> 00:01:37,807
Let me go!

35
00:01:38,474 --> 00:01:39,975
Let me go! You'll pay for this.

36
00:01:40,810 --> 00:01:42,311
Ricardo, come back here!

37
00:01:42,895 --> 00:01:43,896
Let me go!

38
00:01:44,605 --> 00:01:48,317
You won't get away with this!
I'll make you pay!

39
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:49,610
Let me go!

40
00:02:55,843 --> 00:02:57,595
Hey, Patricia. Give me one too.

41
00:02:57,678 --> 00:02:58,804
Thank you.

42
00:02:58,888 --> 00:03:02,766
We told you we should
each make our own copies.

43
00:03:03,642 --> 00:03:07,313
It's cheaper
at the computer shop near my place.

44
00:03:07,938 --> 00:03:09,940
You're amazing, Patricia.

45
00:03:10,024 --> 00:03:11,775
You're juggling so many things at once.

46
00:03:11,859 --> 00:03:14,445
Don't you still have work after class?

47
00:03:14,528 --> 00:03:16,280
Do you even get to rest?

48
00:03:17,281 --> 00:03:18,324
Of course!

49
00:03:18,407 --> 00:03:20,326
-Can you hand these out?
-Sure.

50
00:03:20,409 --> 00:03:22,369
We don't have class every day.

51
00:03:22,453 --> 00:03:24,246
So I just do everything I can
when I have the time.

52
00:03:24,997 --> 00:03:27,458
Buy my toasted buns during break, okay?

53
00:03:27,541 --> 00:03:28,959
-Oh, sure.
-Sure.

54
00:03:29,752 --> 00:03:30,794
I made a lot of copies.

55
00:03:30,878 --> 00:03:33,213
-Good morning.
-Good morning, ma'am.

56
00:03:33,297 --> 00:03:35,633
Good thing you have the handouts now.

57
00:03:36,759 --> 00:03:38,218
You're amazing, Patricia.

58
00:03:38,302 --> 00:03:40,471
Your classmates really
look up to you as a leader.

59
00:03:41,555 --> 00:03:43,182
I'm glad I could help, ma'am.

60
00:03:43,265 --> 00:03:44,892
I make money on the side too.

61
00:03:45,267 --> 00:03:47,478
I can see you're a good organizer.

62
00:03:47,561 --> 00:03:50,689
Would you like
to head the student committee

63
00:03:50,773 --> 00:03:53,651
for our upcoming Entrepreneurship Week?

64
00:03:54,443 --> 00:03:56,278
And this will have credits on your grades.

65
00:03:58,072 --> 00:03:59,782
Sure, ma'am! I'll do it!

66
00:04:00,616 --> 00:04:02,868
I have one more favor to ask.

67
00:04:03,911 --> 00:04:06,372
We would like to send
a letter of invitation

68
00:04:06,455 --> 00:04:07,748
to Ms. Diana Aragon.

69
00:04:08,248 --> 00:04:12,086
We'd like to invite her
to speak at the event.

70
00:04:12,419 --> 00:04:13,963
I hope you can convince her.

71
00:04:16,423 --> 00:04:18,384
Okay, ma'am.

72
00:04:18,467 --> 00:04:20,844
Your mother is an excellent businesswoman.

73
00:04:21,261 --> 00:04:24,014
She's one of the best and most inspiring.

74
00:04:24,098 --> 00:04:27,351
The students could learn so much from her.

75
00:04:31,772 --> 00:04:33,565
-Okay, ma'am.
-Okay.

76
00:04:33,649 --> 00:04:35,150
Okay, let's start!

77
00:04:39,697 --> 00:04:41,532
I want all your decks this afternoon.

78
00:04:41,615 --> 00:04:45,244
And I want them different
from the previous campaign, okay?

79
00:04:45,327 --> 00:04:47,079
Not the slightest detail.

80
00:04:47,162 --> 00:04:48,706
Yes, Ms. D!

81
00:04:48,789 --> 00:04:50,708
I'll check your works later.

82
00:04:51,250 --> 00:04:52,251
Yes, sir.

83
00:04:53,919 --> 00:04:55,504
-Enzo.
-Yes, ma'am?

84
00:04:56,088 --> 00:04:58,465
Where's Patricia?
Does she always come late?

85
00:04:59,258 --> 00:05:01,093
No, Ms. D. It's just for today.

86
00:05:02,511 --> 00:05:03,971
Hasn't she told you?

87
00:05:04,763 --> 00:05:05,806
About what?

88
00:05:07,141 --> 00:05:08,142
Uh…

89
00:05:09,935 --> 00:05:12,187
Patricia, why are you late?

90
00:05:15,357 --> 00:05:17,735
I'm sorry. It won't happen again.

91
00:05:17,818 --> 00:05:20,821
All right. Just go and finish
what you need to do.

92
00:05:20,904 --> 00:05:21,989
Yes, Ms. D.

93
00:05:23,574 --> 00:05:26,076
Ma'am, have you seen the slides
I sent you?

94
00:05:26,618 --> 00:05:27,786
I'll get into it.

95
00:05:27,870 --> 00:05:29,371
Okay, ma'am.

96
00:05:29,455 --> 00:05:30,539
Excuse me.

97
00:05:34,418 --> 00:05:35,586
Enzo.

98
00:05:41,133 --> 00:05:43,302
Is Patricia going through something?

99
00:05:45,763 --> 00:05:47,848
It would be better
if she tells you herself, Ms. D.

100
00:05:47,931 --> 00:05:50,559
Enzo… spill it.

101
00:05:55,189 --> 00:05:56,190
She came from class.

102
00:05:57,483 --> 00:05:59,485
She doesn't want you to know,

103
00:05:59,568 --> 00:06:01,111
but I think you should.

104
00:06:01,987 --> 00:06:03,697
Patricia's gone back to school.

105
00:06:31,391 --> 00:06:32,476
Hey, hey!

106
00:06:35,062 --> 00:06:36,939
-Are you okay?
-Mm-hmm.

107
00:06:37,022 --> 00:06:38,023
It's nothing.

108
00:06:38,107 --> 00:06:39,149
You feel a bit feverish.

109
00:06:39,483 --> 00:06:40,776
No, I'm fine.

110
00:06:41,151 --> 00:06:42,194
Are you sure?

111
00:06:46,782 --> 00:06:48,075
Why are you still here?

112
00:06:50,661 --> 00:06:52,162
I had to finish something.

113
00:06:52,246 --> 00:06:53,664
I was just taking a break.

114
00:06:55,791 --> 00:06:58,001
Please don't tell Ms. D about this.

115
00:06:58,085 --> 00:07:01,296
She might get mad at me again.
I don't want to add on to my sins.

116
00:07:01,380 --> 00:07:05,551
Why don't you just tell her
that you've gone back to school?

117
00:07:06,385 --> 00:07:08,137
She'd understand that.

118
00:07:09,346 --> 00:07:12,349
She might even help you
adjust your schedule.

119
00:07:13,433 --> 00:07:15,477
I don't want any special treatment.

120
00:07:21,567 --> 00:07:22,776
What is it?

121
00:07:22,860 --> 00:07:25,904
Ms. D needs some documents
for Burger City.

122
00:07:25,988 --> 00:07:28,282
She wants them taken to her house tonight.

123
00:07:29,324 --> 00:07:30,409
But I've got something else to do.

124
00:07:31,160 --> 00:07:32,411
I'll do it.

125
00:07:32,744 --> 00:07:35,289
-You don't have to.
-It's okay. You need to rest.

126
00:07:35,372 --> 00:07:38,041
I still need to make up
for my mistakes before.

127
00:07:38,834 --> 00:07:40,335
-Are you sure?
-Yes.

128
00:07:41,211 --> 00:07:43,088
-T-take care.
-Mm.

129
00:07:48,886 --> 00:07:52,306
Oh! Patricia. Come in, come in.

130
00:07:53,098 --> 00:07:54,183
Mm.

131
00:07:57,311 --> 00:07:58,395
Perfect timing.

132
00:07:59,021 --> 00:08:01,106
I just finished cooking.
You should stay for supper.

133
00:08:02,274 --> 00:08:04,151
I'm not here to visit, Nanny Cora.

134
00:08:04,234 --> 00:08:05,235
-Huh?
-It's for work.

135
00:08:05,319 --> 00:08:06,695
I'm going home right after.

136
00:08:08,280 --> 00:08:09,323
But why?

137
00:08:09,865 --> 00:08:11,033
Um…

138
00:08:11,116 --> 00:08:12,993
I just came to deliver
these files to Ms. D.

139
00:08:13,076 --> 00:08:14,161
-Can you give these to her?
-Oh.

140
00:08:14,244 --> 00:08:17,039
Why don't you give those to her yourself?

141
00:08:17,873 --> 00:08:19,041
But…

142
00:08:19,791 --> 00:08:21,293
Are you alright?

143
00:08:22,085 --> 00:08:24,796
I'm fine.
I'm probably just nauseous from the trip.

144
00:08:24,880 --> 00:08:27,382
Oh, you're not fine. Come, have a seat.

145
00:08:27,466 --> 00:08:29,176
Come on. Sit over here. Come on.

146
00:08:29,259 --> 00:08:32,054
Oh-- Oh! Patricia!

147
00:08:32,554 --> 00:08:34,598
Pat-- Help!

148
00:08:34,973 --> 00:08:36,308
Help-- Patricia!

149
00:08:36,391 --> 00:08:37,851
Help! It's Patricia!

150
00:08:37,935 --> 00:08:39,102
-What happened?
-Patricia!

151
00:08:39,186 --> 00:08:40,646
-Patricia!
-What happened?

152
00:08:40,729 --> 00:08:43,273
-What happened? Patricia!
-She suddenly fainted!

153
00:08:43,357 --> 00:08:45,484
-Patricia!
-She's burning up!

154
00:08:45,567 --> 00:08:47,611
Benjie! Benjie!

155
00:08:48,111 --> 00:08:49,279
-Be… Benjie!
-Ms. D?

156
00:08:49,363 --> 00:08:51,365
-Bring her to the guest room.
-Okay.

157
00:09:00,791 --> 00:09:05,379
I HOPE YOU CAN GET
SOME REST NOW. GOOD NIGHT.

158
00:10:52,486 --> 00:10:54,404
I have told you several times.

159
00:10:54,488 --> 00:10:56,615
Quit football!

160
00:10:58,533 --> 00:11:01,495
I've done nothing but work

161
00:11:02,037 --> 00:11:03,497
to feed you!

162
00:11:17,803 --> 00:11:19,012
Mom.

163
00:11:19,096 --> 00:11:20,472
What happened?

164
00:11:20,555 --> 00:11:22,140
I want to go back there.

165
00:11:22,516 --> 00:11:24,476
I want to be with you.

166
00:11:24,559 --> 00:11:26,395
Did your father hit you again?

167
00:11:26,478 --> 00:11:29,189
Mom, didn't you say
you're going to take me from him?

168
00:11:29,523 --> 00:11:30,857
Don't worry, okay?

169
00:11:30,941 --> 00:11:34,611
Mom will do everything
to get you back from your father.

170
00:11:34,945 --> 00:11:39,032
But, son, I can't do it right now.

171
00:11:39,116 --> 00:11:40,534
Just hang in there a bit more.

172
00:11:41,576 --> 00:11:43,120
Mom, I can't do it anymore.

173
00:11:44,037 --> 00:11:47,249
If you put your mind to it,
you can do anything.

174
00:11:47,874 --> 00:11:49,626
Breathe in.

175
00:11:50,794 --> 00:11:52,295
Breathe out.

176
00:12:35,172 --> 00:12:36,173
Ricardo.

177
00:12:39,259 --> 00:12:40,510
I miss you.

178
00:13:03,783 --> 00:13:05,076
Why did you come home?

179
00:13:07,412 --> 00:13:12,125
I traveled all the way from Indonesia.

180
00:13:13,710 --> 00:13:16,630
You didn't even pick me up,
and this is the welcome I get?

181
00:13:17,255 --> 00:13:19,341
I thought you understood the situation.

182
00:13:19,758 --> 00:13:21,009
I do.

183
00:13:21,551 --> 00:13:23,720
But, of course,
I want to spend time with you.

184
00:13:24,763 --> 00:13:26,598
From now on, I'll be staying
in the Philippines.

185
00:13:26,681 --> 00:13:28,308
So that we can be together.

186
00:13:31,811 --> 00:13:34,272
But you know what my plans are, don't you?

187
00:13:42,781 --> 00:13:45,784
Don't worry, I won't stand in your way.

188
00:13:46,743 --> 00:13:49,538
Use me however you want.

189
00:13:50,747 --> 00:13:53,291
I owe you so much.

190
00:13:54,626 --> 00:13:55,961
l will help you.

191
00:14:00,006 --> 00:14:01,633
I'm finally on her good side.

192
00:14:04,135 --> 00:14:06,429
I make her smile even when
she's dealing with problems.

193
00:14:08,557 --> 00:14:11,101
It's like she hasn't ruined any lives.

194
00:14:25,115 --> 00:14:26,408
YOU'RE GOING TO PAY!

195
00:14:26,491 --> 00:14:27,701
WHO'S THIS? I'LL CALL THE COPS!
YOU DON'T SCARE ME!

196
00:14:27,784 --> 00:14:28,994
I'LL FIND YOU! I'LL SUE YOU.

197
00:14:44,801 --> 00:14:47,220
She doesn't know what's coming for her.

198
00:14:48,763 --> 00:14:50,181
I'll take everything from her.

199
00:14:53,310 --> 00:14:55,770
She's going to pay
for what she did to my mother.

200
00:14:58,898 --> 00:15:00,817
Diana isn't easy to break.

201
00:15:03,778 --> 00:15:06,239
But just a little more,
and she'll be mine.

202
00:15:06,323 --> 00:15:09,951
I've worked hard to find my way
into Diana Aragon's life.

203
00:15:13,622 --> 00:15:15,373
Even Patricia, I've already tamed.

204
00:15:16,249 --> 00:15:18,793
I have them in the palm of my hand…

205
00:15:19,419 --> 00:15:22,047
while I make Diana suffer
little by little.

206
00:15:22,130 --> 00:15:25,300
Just like how you
and your mother suffered.

207
00:15:26,051 --> 00:15:27,427
Even worse.

208
00:15:29,346 --> 00:15:32,265
Son, I have some good news for you!

209
00:15:34,392 --> 00:15:40,315
I got into a big company! La Familia!

210
00:15:40,398 --> 00:15:41,399
Really, Mom?

211
00:15:42,150 --> 00:15:43,485
Congratulations, Mom!

212
00:15:43,568 --> 00:15:44,861
My son…

213
00:15:44,944 --> 00:15:47,155
This is the start of a new life for us.

214
00:15:47,739 --> 00:15:49,783
Once everything is settled,

215
00:15:49,866 --> 00:15:53,620
I'll take you home.
We'll be reunited, son.

216
00:15:54,120 --> 00:15:56,164
Mom, I can't wait for that day to come!

217
00:15:56,498 --> 00:16:00,293
My situation here is a bit
complicated right now, son.

218
00:16:01,544 --> 00:16:03,630
But I'll save up.

219
00:16:03,713 --> 00:16:04,839
Mom!

220
00:16:07,801 --> 00:16:11,346
Son, I just need to take care
of something, alright?

221
00:16:11,429 --> 00:16:14,015
I have to look after your siblings.

222
00:16:14,307 --> 00:16:16,393
My husband is arriving soon.

223
00:16:18,853 --> 00:16:19,896
Son…

224
00:16:21,314 --> 00:16:23,441
I'll make it up to you.

225
00:16:24,859 --> 00:16:26,152
It won't be long now.

226
00:16:26,736 --> 00:16:28,780
Just a little more patience, alright?

227
00:16:29,114 --> 00:16:31,491
So that's it. Thank you for today, guys.

228
00:16:33,368 --> 00:16:35,328
Congratulations again, Ricardo.

229
00:16:36,162 --> 00:16:38,498
This is your best work so far.

230
00:16:38,957 --> 00:16:40,083
Thank you.

231
00:16:40,917 --> 00:16:43,503
I'm sure you will
get another promotion soon.

232
00:16:43,586 --> 00:16:44,879
Celebrate tonight?

233
00:16:45,255 --> 00:16:47,716
Thank you, but… probably next time.

234
00:16:48,675 --> 00:16:50,009
-We'll go ahead.
-All right.

235
00:16:50,093 --> 00:16:51,553
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

236
00:16:58,935 --> 00:16:59,936
Hello, Mom?

237
00:17:00,437 --> 00:17:02,647
Is this Cecilia Pineda's son?

238
00:17:03,690 --> 00:17:05,984
I'm calling from Saving Grace Hospital.

239
00:17:06,901 --> 00:17:08,403
Something happened to her.

240
00:17:12,866 --> 00:17:15,410
If no one in your family
started the fire, then who did?

241
00:17:15,827 --> 00:17:17,078
Cecilia Pineda!

242
00:17:17,662 --> 00:17:21,291
A disgruntled employee
who holds a grudge against our company.

243
00:17:21,833 --> 00:17:23,877
A lot of people know this.

244
00:17:24,419 --> 00:17:26,629
We have witnesses testifying against her.

245
00:17:29,716 --> 00:17:31,593
Son, help me.

246
00:17:32,761 --> 00:17:34,846
They're going to put me in prison.

247
00:17:35,221 --> 00:17:36,222
Help me, son.

248
00:17:36,765 --> 00:17:37,974
Mom, you're innocent.

249
00:17:38,433 --> 00:17:42,562
After everything they did to me,
I'm the one who has to suffer?

250
00:17:43,229 --> 00:17:45,315
I won't let them lock you up, Mom.

251
00:17:45,398 --> 00:17:47,108
I'll help you escape.

252
00:17:50,612 --> 00:17:52,113
Son, it hurts so much!

253
00:17:53,239 --> 00:17:54,657
Hang in there, Mom.

254
00:17:54,741 --> 00:17:56,409
The captain has been paid, sir.

255
00:17:56,493 --> 00:17:59,537
We've also informed
our contacts in Indonesia.

256
00:17:59,621 --> 00:18:00,830
But they might ask for more money.

257
00:18:00,914 --> 00:18:02,624
This isn't exactly easy.

258
00:18:02,707 --> 00:18:03,917
Name your price.

259
00:18:04,334 --> 00:18:05,919
Just get us out of this country.

260
00:18:06,002 --> 00:18:09,172
Here are the fake medical
transfer papers you requested.

261
00:18:09,255 --> 00:18:10,965
The other documents are included too, sir.

262
00:18:11,299 --> 00:18:13,802
You're all set now.
The supposed body of your mother

263
00:18:13,885 --> 00:18:16,054
has already been arranged for burial,

264
00:18:16,137 --> 00:18:17,347
so they'll stop coming after you.

265
00:18:19,015 --> 00:18:21,434
Mom, Sandra has already
prepared all that you need.

266
00:18:22,101 --> 00:18:23,728
I have to get to work.

267
00:18:24,270 --> 00:18:26,189
So much time has passed,

268
00:18:27,273 --> 00:18:30,068
but you haven't kept
a single promise to me.

269
00:18:30,944 --> 00:18:33,238
Do you think my life here is easy?

270
00:18:33,863 --> 00:18:37,075
I've been suffering for years, Ricardo.

271
00:18:37,158 --> 00:18:41,371
But they just get to move on
with their lives.

272
00:18:41,454 --> 00:18:43,164
Mom, I'm just taking care of something.

273
00:18:43,581 --> 00:18:46,960
So I'm focusing on your recovery
because you're sick.

274
00:18:47,043 --> 00:18:48,878
i want you to live longer.

275
00:18:49,379 --> 00:18:51,089
What's the point of me living?

276
00:18:52,131 --> 00:18:55,927
The people who did this to me
are living comfortable lives.

277
00:18:56,469 --> 00:18:58,054
Mom, I would do anything for you.

278
00:19:01,391 --> 00:19:03,893
Make sure you stick to our agreement.

279
00:19:04,853 --> 00:19:06,187
You know what you have to do.

280
00:19:07,230 --> 00:19:09,774
Put this in the Cala Soda bottles

281
00:19:09,858 --> 00:19:12,151
that'll be delivered
to the feeding program.

282
00:19:13,111 --> 00:19:15,572
Do a clean job, understand?

283
00:19:16,114 --> 00:19:17,156
Yes, sir.

284
00:19:28,001 --> 00:19:29,794
I can already see her downfall.

285
00:19:32,547 --> 00:19:36,217
I'll make sure she suffers
the way we suffered.

286
00:19:39,512 --> 00:19:42,307
I'll make her suffer
even more than we did.

287
00:19:46,436 --> 00:19:48,438
-Hey, Enzo.
-Nanny Cora.

288
00:19:48,521 --> 00:19:50,356
-Come in.
-Is Patricia still here?

289
00:19:50,440 --> 00:19:53,234
Oh, um, she's burning up with a fever.

290
00:19:53,318 --> 00:19:54,861
She didn't make it home last night.

291
00:19:54,944 --> 00:19:57,196
She's upstairs resting.

292
00:19:57,280 --> 00:19:58,948
-I see.
-Yes.

293
00:20:00,867 --> 00:20:03,244
Enzo, what are you doing here?

294
00:20:03,328 --> 00:20:04,537
Ms. D, good morning.

295
00:20:04,621 --> 00:20:06,122
They're looking for Patricia at her place.

296
00:20:06,205 --> 00:20:08,625
I just came by to check on her.
Is everything okay?

297
00:20:08,708 --> 00:20:10,376
I've already informed her father.

298
00:20:11,419 --> 00:20:12,587
Is there anything I can do?

299
00:20:12,670 --> 00:20:15,298
I can go out.
I can buy medicine, food, anything.

300
00:20:15,381 --> 00:20:17,300
No, it's okay, Enzo.

301
00:20:17,383 --> 00:20:19,052
We'll take care of Patricia.

302
00:20:19,636 --> 00:20:21,179
You can go back to La Familia.

303
00:20:38,196 --> 00:20:42,575
Did you come here for me… or for Patricia?

304
00:20:44,702 --> 00:20:47,246
I'm just worried about Patricia, Ms. D.

305
00:20:48,915 --> 00:20:50,708
Because?

306
00:20:51,459 --> 00:20:54,087
Because she's sick.

307
00:20:55,546 --> 00:20:57,048
Because?

308
00:20:57,674 --> 00:20:58,883
Because…

309
00:21:03,137 --> 00:21:04,472
Well, Ms. D, I…

310
00:21:06,182 --> 00:21:07,433
I care for your daughter.

311
00:21:08,226 --> 00:21:10,269
And why?

312
00:21:11,104 --> 00:21:12,313
I like her, Ms. D.

313
00:21:13,856 --> 00:21:14,983
I like Patricia.

314
00:21:17,527 --> 00:21:19,237
This is not the right time.

315
00:21:19,988 --> 00:21:22,615
Patricia has a lot of things
to fix in her life.

316
00:21:23,408 --> 00:21:25,368
Don't make it complicated.

317
00:21:25,827 --> 00:21:26,869
Don't go there.

318
00:21:27,662 --> 00:21:28,746
Hm?

319
00:21:29,455 --> 00:21:31,582
With all due respect, Ms. D…

320
00:21:36,671 --> 00:21:39,841
I'm just telling you this to inform you.

321
00:21:40,383 --> 00:21:43,302
I think we are at the right age.

322
00:21:43,761 --> 00:21:48,016
And I think Patricia should be
the one to make those decisions.

323
00:21:52,061 --> 00:21:54,605
Go back to La Familia.

324
00:22:01,112 --> 00:22:04,115
Here's Patricia's phone.
She forgot it in the office.

325
00:22:09,120 --> 00:22:10,538
Have a great day, Ms. D.

326
00:22:26,554 --> 00:22:28,556
Oh, Martin, where are you going?

327
00:22:28,639 --> 00:22:31,768
To the mansion.
Patricia's there, and she has a fever.

328
00:22:34,270 --> 00:22:37,982
Come on, you.
Patricia's not a kid anymore.

329
00:22:38,066 --> 00:22:42,070
Plus, I'm sure you'll just fight
with Diana when you see each other.

330
00:22:42,904 --> 00:22:45,323
It's not like I can just
leave her all alone.

331
00:22:45,406 --> 00:22:46,908
Why? Is her condition that bad?

332
00:22:47,742 --> 00:22:48,826
Don't get me started.

333
00:22:52,497 --> 00:22:55,792
Are you really going there for Patricia?

334
00:22:56,834 --> 00:22:58,169
Or Diana?

335
00:22:58,252 --> 00:23:00,213
What is this? A family reunion?

336
00:23:00,296 --> 00:23:04,926
You're both going to take care
of your beloved daughter?

337
00:23:08,054 --> 00:23:10,473
What? Martin.

338
00:24:18,416 --> 00:24:19,750
Patricia.

339
00:24:20,918 --> 00:24:25,006
Why did you get up?
You're still recovering.

340
00:24:25,590 --> 00:24:26,716
I'm fine.

341
00:24:28,301 --> 00:24:29,385
What happened?

342
00:24:29,927 --> 00:24:31,179
You fainted.

343
00:24:31,846 --> 00:24:33,598
Your fever was so high last night.

344
00:24:33,681 --> 00:24:35,308
My gosh. Here.

345
00:24:35,975 --> 00:24:38,519
We prepared some breakfast for you.
Eat it first.

346
00:24:38,603 --> 00:24:40,479
When you finish, change into these, okay?

347
00:24:40,563 --> 00:24:41,772
Come. Eat up.

348
00:24:41,856 --> 00:24:42,982
Goodness me.

349
00:24:43,482 --> 00:24:45,943
-Come!
-Oh, you shouldn't have bothered, Nanny.

350
00:24:46,027 --> 00:24:47,028
Mm-hmm?

351
00:24:49,947 --> 00:24:51,157
Oh, no.

352
00:24:51,407 --> 00:24:53,492
Ms. D will surely get mad at you.

353
00:24:54,118 --> 00:24:55,328
You know how she is.

354
00:24:55,411 --> 00:24:57,205
She doesn't like the smell of dried fish.

355
00:24:57,288 --> 00:24:59,332
I even troubled you last night.

356
00:24:59,790 --> 00:25:01,792
What are you even talking about?

357
00:25:02,335 --> 00:25:04,629
Diana requested this herself.

358
00:25:04,712 --> 00:25:06,631
She told us to cook for you

359
00:25:06,714 --> 00:25:08,758
because she knows these are your favorite.

360
00:25:08,841 --> 00:25:10,176
Go on, eat up.

361
00:25:23,564 --> 00:25:24,732
Mmm.

362
00:25:27,485 --> 00:25:29,362
Were you the one
who took care of me last night?

363
00:25:31,030 --> 00:25:32,240
I'm sorry for the trouble I've caused you

364
00:25:32,740 --> 00:25:34,075
but thank you.

365
00:25:34,158 --> 00:25:36,118
Don't thank me.

366
00:25:37,036 --> 00:25:38,329
Thank your mother.

367
00:25:38,955 --> 00:25:40,915
She's the one who took care of you.

368
00:25:41,958 --> 00:25:44,168
She even slept by your side.

369
00:25:44,252 --> 00:25:46,837
All night long, she looked after you.

370
00:25:53,177 --> 00:25:54,679
I'll show you something.

371
00:25:55,596 --> 00:25:56,597
Here.

372
00:26:05,022 --> 00:26:06,274
I'll head in first.

373
00:26:25,459 --> 00:26:27,336
No matter how many years have passed,

374
00:26:28,379 --> 00:26:30,089
she didn't change anything.

375
00:26:31,507 --> 00:26:33,426
Not a single thing.

376
00:26:35,052 --> 00:26:39,765
She wanted this room to stay the same way
as you last saw it.

377
00:26:53,446 --> 00:26:56,198
Maybe there's something in here
that you like.

378
00:26:56,657 --> 00:26:57,742
You can take it home.

379
00:26:58,826 --> 00:27:00,494
It's yours anyway.

380
00:27:00,578 --> 00:27:02,413
I'll talk to your mother.

381
00:28:11,732 --> 00:28:13,442
Why are you here?

382
00:28:25,746 --> 00:28:27,123
Where's…

383
00:28:27,957 --> 00:28:29,834
Nanny Cora?

384
00:28:41,178 --> 00:28:42,680
My room hasn't changed at all.

385
00:28:48,436 --> 00:28:49,937
I didn't change anything.

386
00:28:51,021 --> 00:28:52,606
In case you came back.

387
00:28:55,901 --> 00:28:58,195
But I didn't expect that…

388
00:29:00,030 --> 00:29:02,283
we'd be separated for so long.

389
00:29:05,494 --> 00:29:08,914
It's been a while since…
I last went in here.

390
00:29:19,633 --> 00:29:20,926
It's a waste of space.

391
00:29:22,219 --> 00:29:24,346
You could've turned it
into your home office.

392
00:29:26,640 --> 00:29:28,392
I want you to have somewhere to return to.

393
00:29:44,992 --> 00:29:46,243
Uh…

394
00:29:49,538 --> 00:29:51,415
You're the one
who took care of me last night?

395
00:29:55,628 --> 00:29:57,713
I'm sorry for causing you trouble.

396
00:30:01,592 --> 00:30:02,718
But thank you.

397
00:30:04,803 --> 00:30:06,096
I know…

398
00:30:08,307 --> 00:30:11,435
I wasn't a good mother to you.

399
00:30:14,355 --> 00:30:16,440
But I hope you believe that…

400
00:30:17,441 --> 00:30:18,776
I tried.

401
00:30:21,445 --> 00:30:23,239
It may not have been enough.

402
00:30:26,700 --> 00:30:31,163
But that doesn't mean that I haven't…
fought for you.

403
00:30:42,800 --> 00:30:44,218
Where's my daughter, Cora?

404
00:30:44,718 --> 00:30:45,970
Call your boss.

405
00:30:46,053 --> 00:30:47,805
Martin, just wait.

406
00:30:47,888 --> 00:30:51,016
-They're going down.
-Don't say too much. Call your boss!

407
00:30:53,227 --> 00:30:54,895
-Dad.
-Patricia.

408
00:30:56,605 --> 00:30:58,190
What are you doing here?

409
00:31:00,317 --> 00:31:02,987
You should've just taken Patricia home.

410
00:31:03,571 --> 00:31:04,572
I can take care of her.

411
00:31:04,655 --> 00:31:06,282
I can get her treated.

412
00:31:06,365 --> 00:31:08,492
We don't need to argue about this.

413
00:31:08,576 --> 00:31:10,077
Just say it,

414
00:31:11,036 --> 00:31:13,122
you just want to rub it to my face

415
00:31:13,205 --> 00:31:15,791
that I can't take care of Patricia.

416
00:31:16,625 --> 00:31:17,835
Right?

417
00:31:17,918 --> 00:31:19,169
What are you trying to pull?

418
00:31:19,253 --> 00:31:23,299
I'll do what I did
as many times as I have to for Patricia.

419
00:31:24,216 --> 00:31:25,759
Maybe you've forgotten.

420
00:31:26,385 --> 00:31:30,222
We're living this kind of life
because of you.

421
00:31:30,306 --> 00:31:31,348
Because you abandoned us.

422
00:31:31,890 --> 00:31:34,226
Patricia begged you back then, didn't she?

423
00:31:34,310 --> 00:31:35,686
But what did you do?

424
00:31:35,769 --> 00:31:36,937
You drove her away.

425
00:31:38,147 --> 00:31:40,774
You even dragged our child
into your anger toward me.

426
00:31:40,858 --> 00:31:42,860
And now, you're going to pretend

427
00:31:43,360 --> 00:31:44,570
to be the perfect mother.

428
00:31:48,490 --> 00:31:50,409
You don't know the truth, Martin.

429
00:31:50,993 --> 00:31:52,286
What do you mean, "I don't know"?

430
00:31:52,369 --> 00:31:55,080
Now you're painting me
a liar in front of Patricia?

431
00:32:04,965 --> 00:32:06,550
I helped you, Martin.

432
00:32:07,343 --> 00:32:09,178
Because my daughter asked for it.

433
00:32:14,808 --> 00:32:16,268
What do you mean?

434
00:32:18,270 --> 00:32:20,689
Diana, Martin got into an accident!

435
00:32:26,612 --> 00:32:27,946
Mom, let's go. Let's go!

436
00:32:28,030 --> 00:32:29,782
-They don't want us here!
-No, wait!

437
00:32:29,865 --> 00:32:31,075
They don't want us!

438
00:32:31,158 --> 00:32:34,370
-Diana!
-Please leave, Carlota.

439
00:32:34,453 --> 00:32:36,538
Please, Diana!

440
00:32:36,622 --> 00:32:37,706
Mom, let's go!

441
00:32:42,461 --> 00:32:43,754
Diana.

442
00:32:43,837 --> 00:32:44,922
What does she need?

443
00:32:45,005 --> 00:32:46,882
She said Martin got into an accident.

444
00:32:46,965 --> 00:32:50,135
She stole my husband,
now she'll come to me for help?

445
00:32:52,471 --> 00:32:55,099
You didn't see Patricia.

446
00:32:57,643 --> 00:32:58,727
Patricia?

447
00:32:59,645 --> 00:33:01,730
-Is she there?
-They've already left.

448
00:33:03,941 --> 00:33:05,442
Carlota Cervantes?

449
00:33:09,947 --> 00:33:13,158
Ma'am Diana Aragon sent these
for Sir Martin.

450
00:33:13,242 --> 00:33:14,493
For his operation.

451
00:33:14,576 --> 00:33:16,745
-These are from Diana?
-Yes.

452
00:33:16,829 --> 00:33:18,831
-Thank you.
-You're welcome.

453
00:33:29,049 --> 00:33:30,092
That's not true!

454
00:33:30,676 --> 00:33:31,844
You're losing your mind.

455
00:33:32,469 --> 00:33:35,889
Carlota was the one who found a way
to help me.

456
00:33:37,433 --> 00:33:38,600
Then ask her.

457
00:33:41,186 --> 00:33:42,730
Come on, dear. Let's leave.

458
00:33:48,944 --> 00:33:50,070
Patricia!

459
00:33:59,496 --> 00:34:00,706
Thank you.

460
00:34:23,645 --> 00:34:24,897
Carlota!

461
00:34:29,193 --> 00:34:30,944
I'm glad you're home.

462
00:34:31,028 --> 00:34:32,905
Patricia, are you still sick?

463
00:34:34,948 --> 00:34:36,074
Jena, leave us alone for now.

464
00:34:41,747 --> 00:34:43,916
Carlota, let's talk.

465
00:34:43,999 --> 00:34:45,959
What do you want to talk about?

466
00:34:46,043 --> 00:34:47,044
Hm?

467
00:34:49,588 --> 00:34:51,799
You want to talk

468
00:34:51,882 --> 00:34:54,426
about how you and Diana reconciled?

469
00:34:55,010 --> 00:34:56,678
Is that what his is about?

470
00:34:56,762 --> 00:34:58,180
-Tell me--
-From whom…

471
00:34:58,639 --> 00:35:00,974
and where did you really get the money

472
00:35:01,058 --> 00:35:02,601
for my hospital bills?

473
00:35:02,684 --> 00:35:05,729
Why do you keep bringing that up?

474
00:35:05,813 --> 00:35:08,607
Didn't I tell you before?

475
00:35:09,107 --> 00:35:11,527
I borrowed money from my acquaintances.

476
00:35:11,610 --> 00:35:13,237
I did everything I could.

477
00:35:13,320 --> 00:35:17,324
I lined up, I-- I sought help
from the government.

478
00:35:17,407 --> 00:35:18,784
Who did you borrow from?

479
00:35:19,451 --> 00:35:20,702
What is this?

480
00:35:20,786 --> 00:35:23,539
What? Do you want a name?
Do you want a list?

481
00:35:23,622 --> 00:35:25,415
Do you want me to name them one by one?

482
00:35:25,499 --> 00:35:26,792
-Huh?
-Diana said…

483
00:35:26,875 --> 00:35:29,670
-What?
-she gave you the money.

484
00:35:30,128 --> 00:35:33,090
You made us believe
that she didn't help Dad.

485
00:35:40,180 --> 00:35:41,431
Fine!

486
00:35:42,349 --> 00:35:43,725
All right!

487
00:35:43,809 --> 00:35:45,602
Fine, the money came from her.

488
00:35:45,686 --> 00:35:48,730
But that doesn't erase
how terrible she was.

489
00:35:49,147 --> 00:35:50,816
She abandoned you.

490
00:35:50,899 --> 00:35:52,067
But me?

491
00:35:53,277 --> 00:35:56,363
I spent almost my whole life
devoted to you!

492
00:35:56,446 --> 00:35:57,990
I took care of you.

493
00:35:58,073 --> 00:35:59,908
I sacrificed so many years for you,

494
00:35:59,992 --> 00:36:01,952
and this is how you repay me?

495
00:36:02,035 --> 00:36:03,537
You're going to throw it in my face?

496
00:36:04,121 --> 00:36:05,789
It wouldn't have gotten this bad

497
00:36:05,873 --> 00:36:07,666
-if you had told us the truth!
-Fine, then! Fine!

498
00:36:07,749 --> 00:36:09,918
Fine! Take each other's side!

499
00:36:10,002 --> 00:36:14,214
Go back to her if what I did was so wrong!

500
00:36:14,840 --> 00:36:16,842
If you think I've never
done anything right,

501
00:36:16,925 --> 00:36:20,512
then fine! I'll be the villain!

502
00:36:32,232 --> 00:36:34,568
Diana. What's happening?

503
00:36:35,527 --> 00:36:37,362
I don't know what you're accusing me of.

504
00:36:37,446 --> 00:36:38,697
I didn't do anything wrong.

505
00:36:38,780 --> 00:36:40,449
The evidence against you is clear, Teddy.

506
00:36:40,532 --> 00:36:42,284
Face the investigation. Prove to them…

507
00:36:42,367 --> 00:36:45,120
-that you're innocent.
-Why won't you believe me?

508
00:36:45,746 --> 00:36:47,497
I'm your brother. I'm your family.

509
00:36:47,581 --> 00:36:49,666
Why does what other people say
matter more to you?

510
00:36:49,750 --> 00:36:52,961
Family? Why? Since when has that
become important to you?

511
00:36:53,045 --> 00:36:55,547
You don't even listen to my side!

512
00:36:55,964 --> 00:36:56,965
Come on!

513
00:36:57,382 --> 00:36:59,092
I gave you so many chances.

514
00:36:59,176 --> 00:37:02,596
And each time, you have proven me wrong!

515
00:37:02,679 --> 00:37:05,015
When did you ever trust me?

516
00:37:05,098 --> 00:37:07,809
Even then, no matter what I do,
you're always doubting me.

517
00:37:08,226 --> 00:37:11,063
You treat every mistake
like it's a mortal sin.

518
00:37:11,146 --> 00:37:12,731
Like it'll ruin your whole world.

519
00:37:13,065 --> 00:37:16,068
Have I ever done
anything right in your eyes?

520
00:37:16,151 --> 00:37:17,945
Don't turn this around on me, Teddy.

521
00:37:19,196 --> 00:37:20,948
You're no different than Dad.

522
00:37:22,908 --> 00:37:24,076
That's why Mom left him.

523
00:37:25,077 --> 00:37:26,453
He's evil to the core.

524
00:37:27,746 --> 00:37:30,415
Aren't you afraid
you'll end up just like him?

525
00:37:30,499 --> 00:37:31,917
Oh, wait! I'm sorry.

526
00:37:33,168 --> 00:37:34,211
You already are!

527
00:37:35,295 --> 00:37:36,630
Even worse!

528
00:37:38,882 --> 00:37:41,176
Since you were a child,
I was the one who took care of you.

529
00:37:41,593 --> 00:37:42,928
But you never saw that.

530
00:37:43,303 --> 00:37:45,639
Because you never saw me as your sister,

531
00:37:45,722 --> 00:37:47,182
but only as your competition!

532
00:37:53,063 --> 00:37:54,648
What's on your mind?

533
00:37:57,025 --> 00:37:59,277
You've been deep in thought for a while.

534
00:37:59,987 --> 00:38:03,115
I thought she had completely
erased me from her life.

535
00:38:06,451 --> 00:38:08,954
I resented her for so long, Enzo.

536
00:38:14,001 --> 00:38:16,003
But all this time…

537
00:38:19,881 --> 00:38:22,009
she was just waiting for me to come home.

538
00:38:30,434 --> 00:38:34,730
Sometimes, you just have
to be open, Patricia.

539
00:38:39,359 --> 00:38:40,944
Does that mean…

540
00:38:42,237 --> 00:38:43,405
you two are okay now?

541
00:38:51,496 --> 00:38:52,831
Not right away.

542
00:38:57,210 --> 00:38:58,754
But I'll try.

543
00:39:29,326 --> 00:39:31,328
-Good morning.
-Good morning.

544
00:39:32,704 --> 00:39:33,747
For you.

545
00:39:35,874 --> 00:39:36,958
What's this?

546
00:39:37,793 --> 00:39:39,252
Vitamins.

547
00:39:39,795 --> 00:39:40,796
Oh.

548
00:39:41,463 --> 00:39:42,672
Thank you.

549
00:39:45,550 --> 00:39:47,219
How are you feeling?

550
00:39:48,178 --> 00:39:51,014
I'm okay now. You don't have to worry.

551
00:39:56,269 --> 00:39:57,354
You're…

552
00:39:58,105 --> 00:39:59,523
You're back in school?

553
00:40:02,484 --> 00:40:03,860
How did you…

554
00:40:03,944 --> 00:40:05,695
Enzo told me.

555
00:40:07,989 --> 00:40:09,825
Can you juggle both work and school?

556
00:40:11,076 --> 00:40:12,869
Just let me know.

557
00:40:12,953 --> 00:40:16,414
We can arrange a special schedule
to accommodate your studies.

558
00:40:16,790 --> 00:40:18,625
Oh no, that's not necessary.

559
00:40:18,708 --> 00:40:19,960
I've got it figured out.

560
00:40:20,544 --> 00:40:22,337
Uh…

561
00:40:22,420 --> 00:40:25,715
I know this is late, but…

562
00:40:28,135 --> 00:40:31,054
I wanted to say thank you
for helping with my dad.

563
00:40:35,767 --> 00:40:37,435
He could've been left disabled

564
00:40:37,519 --> 00:40:39,396
-if you hadn't helped him.
-Oh.

565
00:40:39,479 --> 00:40:40,730
Patricia…

566
00:40:41,273 --> 00:40:42,858
Let's forget about that.

567
00:40:43,316 --> 00:40:44,526
Let's just move on.

568
00:40:50,365 --> 00:40:52,075
You're right. Move on.

569
00:40:52,159 --> 00:40:57,122
If there's anything I can help with
or if you need anything,

570
00:40:57,205 --> 00:40:58,290
please let me know.

571
00:41:00,584 --> 00:41:03,044
To be honest, I do need something.

572
00:41:03,128 --> 00:41:04,796
Good thing, you asked.

573
00:41:05,255 --> 00:41:07,299
What? Tell me.

574
00:41:08,175 --> 00:41:09,551
It's…

575
00:41:12,262 --> 00:41:15,682
There's a school activity
that I was assigned to.

576
00:41:16,141 --> 00:41:17,851
It's for our Entrepreneurship Week.

577
00:41:17,934 --> 00:41:19,144
-Ah!
-Uh…

578
00:41:19,853 --> 00:41:22,564
I wanted to invite you there.

579
00:41:24,065 --> 00:41:28,320
Just tell me when
and I'll adjust my schedule.

580
00:41:30,030 --> 00:41:31,198
You'd do that?

581
00:41:31,281 --> 00:41:32,324
Yes!

582
00:41:32,782 --> 00:41:35,118
-Thank you.
-You're welcome.

583
00:41:37,370 --> 00:41:38,955
I'll see you later?

584
00:41:39,039 --> 00:41:40,207
-Yes.
-Okay.

585
00:42:13,365 --> 00:42:14,741
Uncle Teddy?

586
00:42:16,284 --> 00:42:17,744
I just want to talk to you.

587
00:42:18,870 --> 00:42:19,996
Listen to me.

588
00:42:20,622 --> 00:42:21,957
Talk to my sister for me.

589
00:42:23,083 --> 00:42:25,043
Tell her I am not guilty.

590
00:42:25,835 --> 00:42:27,671
Uncle Teddy,
if she doesn't believe in you,

591
00:42:27,754 --> 00:42:29,339
I can't do anything about it.

592
00:42:29,422 --> 00:42:31,508
This is all Ricardo's doing!

593
00:42:31,591 --> 00:42:34,010
He's the one to blame!
He's spreading rumors about me!

594
00:42:34,094 --> 00:42:35,387
He framed me,

595
00:42:35,470 --> 00:42:37,681
he set me up, he was the one to blame!

596
00:42:37,764 --> 00:42:39,057
Not me!

597
00:42:39,140 --> 00:42:40,934
Why would I believe you?

598
00:42:42,018 --> 00:42:44,437
And why would Sir Ricardo do that to you?

599
00:42:46,356 --> 00:42:49,442
I don't know. All I know is he has a plan.

600
00:42:49,526 --> 00:42:53,446
So, you want me to talk to Ms. D
because of your hunch?

601
00:42:53,530 --> 00:42:56,408
I just know that he wanted
me gone from La Familia.

602
00:42:59,035 --> 00:43:00,578
Patricia, I'm innocent.

603
00:43:01,871 --> 00:43:05,250
What if you don't really know Ricardo?

604
00:43:22,559 --> 00:43:25,020
I guess Sir Teddy must be so desperate

605
00:43:25,687 --> 00:43:27,105
to talk to you about that.

606
00:43:29,149 --> 00:43:30,859
But why was he saying that Sir Ricardo

607
00:43:30,942 --> 00:43:32,319
was the one framing him?

608
00:43:34,529 --> 00:43:37,157
No. That would be weird.

609
00:43:37,240 --> 00:43:38,950
Why would Sir Ricardo do that?

610
00:43:39,868 --> 00:43:41,161
Before he got in La Familia,

611
00:43:41,244 --> 00:43:43,163
Ms. D and I did a background check on him.

612
00:43:43,663 --> 00:43:46,041
I didn't see anything
questionable about him.

613
00:43:50,462 --> 00:43:55,175
I know that Uncle Teddy
has every reason to lie.

614
00:43:55,675 --> 00:43:59,304
But Enzo, are we going
to disregard his hunch?

615
00:44:00,638 --> 00:44:02,682
You, Patricia…

616
00:44:02,766 --> 00:44:05,060
-Mm?
-Come here.

617
00:44:05,143 --> 00:44:06,853
Sit here. Give me that.

618
00:44:07,937 --> 00:44:09,606
You need to take a break.

619
00:44:10,440 --> 00:44:11,316
Here it is.

620
00:44:11,399 --> 00:44:13,610
Will you add that to your to-do list too?

621
00:44:14,527 --> 00:44:17,697
You just got better. Take a break.

622
00:44:18,782 --> 00:44:20,158
I don't have time to rest.

623
00:44:20,241 --> 00:44:23,411
I have a lot of work
and schoolwork waiting for me.

624
00:44:24,662 --> 00:44:27,582
Well, at least you get to spend time
with Ms. D without working.

625
00:44:29,584 --> 00:44:31,127
Are you taking your vitamins?

626
00:44:31,669 --> 00:44:33,421
Don't push yourself too hard, huh?

627
00:44:33,505 --> 00:44:35,090
Especially for your studies.

628
00:44:35,715 --> 00:44:36,841
Just call me.

629
00:44:36,925 --> 00:44:38,843
I can help you on your
Entrepreneurship Week.

630
00:44:39,219 --> 00:44:41,471
You worry too much!

631
00:44:41,554 --> 00:44:43,848
I still have both my hands and feet.
I can handle it.

632
00:44:43,932 --> 00:44:45,308
You're overreacting.

633
00:44:45,392 --> 00:44:46,810
Is it wrong to worry about you?

634
00:44:50,188 --> 00:44:51,022
It's not that.

635
00:44:51,523 --> 00:44:52,857
Vitamins. Okay?

636
00:44:53,691 --> 00:44:54,984
And let me know if you need help.

637
00:45:14,462 --> 00:45:16,965
Melody, I'll go there early.

638
00:45:17,048 --> 00:45:20,218
Yes. Everything should be ready
for the Entrepreneurship Week.

639
00:45:21,719 --> 00:45:23,805
There's still things missing?

640
00:45:24,514 --> 00:45:27,767
Oh, well, that'll do.
I'll just do a follow-up tomorrow.

641
00:45:28,435 --> 00:45:30,979
Okay, okay. Thank you. Bye.

642
00:45:37,610 --> 00:45:39,195
Ah. Nothing.

643
00:45:40,363 --> 00:45:41,990
Coffee doesn't suffice, huh?

644
00:46:00,925 --> 00:46:02,469
You're cute, huh?

645
00:46:03,428 --> 00:46:05,263
Just a bit OCD.

646
00:46:06,097 --> 00:46:07,432
But reliable.

647
00:46:10,393 --> 00:46:11,478
A gentleman.

648
00:46:12,520 --> 00:46:13,605
Someone I can lean on.

649
00:46:14,147 --> 00:46:16,149
You even understand my craziness.

650
00:46:16,691 --> 00:46:21,696
It's like you always know
what to say when I get dramatic.

651
00:46:29,370 --> 00:46:30,622
What was that?

652
00:46:30,705 --> 00:46:32,290
Ah, nothing! That's uh…

653
00:46:32,373 --> 00:46:33,708
Those are my lines.

654
00:46:33,791 --> 00:46:35,418
I'm rehearsing for my audition.

655
00:46:35,502 --> 00:46:37,170
-Lines?
-Mm-hmm.

656
00:46:37,253 --> 00:46:39,297
-Nice lines, huh?
-Mm-hmm.

657
00:46:41,841 --> 00:46:44,719
Maybe, I can audition there too.

658
00:46:45,470 --> 00:46:46,513
For what role?

659
00:46:48,806 --> 00:46:49,849
As your boyfriend.

660
00:46:50,767 --> 00:46:51,809
Really?

661
00:46:55,939 --> 00:46:57,315
Sir Enzo.

662
00:46:58,566 --> 00:46:59,609
Boyfriend?

663
00:47:12,830 --> 00:47:14,207
But seriously.

664
00:47:18,586 --> 00:47:19,879
You want to give it a try?

665
00:47:27,095 --> 00:47:28,888
-I'll go ahead, I'm late!
-Yes, go ahead.

666
00:47:28,972 --> 00:47:31,307
Jena, I told you to arrange
the groceries last night!

667
00:47:31,391 --> 00:47:33,142
I already bought it.
All you have to do is arrange it!

668
00:47:33,226 --> 00:47:34,936
-Sis, I have school!
-Arrange it now!

669
00:47:35,019 --> 00:47:36,479
I can't take care of that now!

670
00:47:36,563 --> 00:47:38,147
I also have school! I even have an event.

671
00:47:38,231 --> 00:47:39,857
It's important that I'm there early.

672
00:47:39,941 --> 00:47:41,442
It's hard to commute. It's rush hour!

673
00:47:41,526 --> 00:47:42,777
-Please, Jena!
-Patricia, I will meet

674
00:47:42,860 --> 00:47:44,696
some friends so I can't be late!

675
00:47:44,779 --> 00:47:47,574
Mom will get angry
if she sees the groceries lying there!

676
00:47:47,657 --> 00:47:48,866
-Please, Jena.
-Hello.

677
00:47:48,950 --> 00:47:50,743
-Where's Patricia?
-It's hard to get a ride!

678
00:47:50,827 --> 00:47:52,036
-She's there.
-I'll fix it later!

679
00:47:52,120 --> 00:47:54,581
Sis, I think you don't need
to commute anymore.

680
00:47:54,664 --> 00:47:56,916
-Ah.
-I think you have a ride.

681
00:47:58,960 --> 00:48:00,253
Sis!

682
00:48:00,336 --> 00:48:02,338
He brought flowers!

683
00:48:02,797 --> 00:48:06,718
He's handsome! Sis, go there!

684
00:48:11,014 --> 00:48:12,515
Mm-hmm.

685
00:48:17,312 --> 00:48:18,313
Hi.

686
00:48:19,564 --> 00:48:20,607
Hello!

687
00:48:21,733 --> 00:48:22,775
What is that for?

688
00:48:25,028 --> 00:48:26,112
Nothing.

689
00:48:26,863 --> 00:48:28,114
I just wanted to make your day.

690
00:48:39,125 --> 00:48:40,293
Thank you.

691
00:48:42,128 --> 00:48:43,379
Let's go?

692
00:48:47,133 --> 00:48:49,719
-Hey, maybe we can get a ride too?
-Sis?

693
00:48:51,137 --> 00:48:52,889
-Absolutely. Let's go!
-Come on! Let's go!

694
00:48:52,972 --> 00:48:55,808
-Close the gate!
-Oh no.

695
00:49:12,659 --> 00:49:14,077
-Wait a second.
-Mm?

696
00:49:16,996 --> 00:49:18,206
For you.

697
00:49:18,289 --> 00:49:19,290
What is this?

698
00:49:19,707 --> 00:49:21,042
Open it!

699
00:49:27,548 --> 00:49:29,926
YES, YOU PASSED THE AUDITION!

700
00:49:33,638 --> 00:49:35,431
-Yes?
-Yes!

701
00:49:36,099 --> 00:49:38,559
-Yes!
-Hey, hey!

702
00:49:39,185 --> 00:49:40,937
That's your talent fee for now.

703
00:49:49,278 --> 00:49:51,989
Uh, my name is Enzo.

704
00:49:52,073 --> 00:49:53,533
Hi, Bro Enzo. I'm Jena.

705
00:49:53,616 --> 00:49:54,951
I'm April.

706
00:49:55,034 --> 00:49:56,077
Hello.

707
00:50:14,387 --> 00:50:17,223
You and Patricia seem to be okay now.

708
00:50:19,225 --> 00:50:22,937
You know, I'm glad that
she's listening to me somehow.

709
00:50:24,981 --> 00:50:28,192
Oh! I have to go. I'm so sorry.
I don't have time to talk, Ricardo.

710
00:50:28,276 --> 00:50:30,194
I have to go to Patricia.

711
00:50:31,070 --> 00:50:32,321
Okay.

712
00:50:32,405 --> 00:50:34,615
I have to give a talk at her school.

713
00:50:34,699 --> 00:50:35,783
Mm.

714
00:50:47,253 --> 00:50:49,589
I KNOW ABOUT EVERY MOVE
YOU MAKE. BE CAREFUL.

715
00:51:01,684 --> 00:51:03,519
-Diana, what's the matter?
-Um…

716
00:51:04,270 --> 00:51:06,939
Those bastards!
They're intimidating me again.

717
00:51:07,857 --> 00:51:08,858
I'll call the police then.

718
00:51:08,941 --> 00:51:10,777
No, no. I have to go.

719
00:51:10,860 --> 00:51:12,236
I have to go to Patricia.

720
00:51:13,279 --> 00:51:15,198
Wait! What if it wasn't just a phone call?

721
00:51:15,281 --> 00:51:16,699
What if someone is waiting
for you out there?

722
00:51:16,783 --> 00:51:19,285
Let's wait for the police
so that they can assess the threat.

723
00:51:19,368 --> 00:51:21,871
No! If I wait, it will be too late.

724
00:51:21,954 --> 00:51:24,957
I can't let Patricia down, Ricardo.
Not this time.

725
00:51:26,292 --> 00:51:27,835
Enzo, is she still coming?

726
00:51:28,544 --> 00:51:30,129
Ms. D said she's on her way.

727
00:51:30,713 --> 00:51:32,340
We still have 30 minutes left.

728
00:51:32,423 --> 00:51:35,885
You know that she always arrives one hour
before an event starts, right?

729
00:51:37,345 --> 00:51:38,805
Maybe she just had to deal
with something first.

730
00:51:39,847 --> 00:51:41,057
Enzo…

731
00:51:41,140 --> 00:51:42,767
Hey, hey, hey.

732
00:51:43,851 --> 00:51:47,063
Relax. She will come, okay?

733
00:51:47,480 --> 00:51:50,525
-Wait, I'll go wait for her outside, okay?
-All right.

734
00:51:56,489 --> 00:51:58,449
Benjie, what's taking you so long?

735
00:51:58,533 --> 00:52:00,743
Ms. D, it looks like
there was an accident.

736
00:52:00,827 --> 00:52:01,953
What?

737
00:52:08,000 --> 00:52:09,001
Ms. D!

738
00:52:09,627 --> 00:52:11,462
You crashed into my car!

739
00:52:12,463 --> 00:52:14,465
-What will you do now?
-It's your fault!

740
00:52:14,549 --> 00:52:16,217
-Ms. Dela Cruz.
-Ma'am.

741
00:52:16,300 --> 00:52:17,677
Is Ms. Aragon already on her way?

742
00:52:19,053 --> 00:52:22,056
Uh, I'll try calling her again.

743
00:52:22,723 --> 00:52:24,976
-Okay. Thank you.
-Sorry, ma'am.

744
00:52:25,768 --> 00:52:28,145
Hi, are we all good?

745
00:52:59,719 --> 00:53:00,761
HAPPY MOTHER'S DAY

746
00:53:09,520 --> 00:53:10,605
Patricia!

747
00:53:13,274 --> 00:53:14,358
I'm here.

748
00:53:25,995 --> 00:53:28,873
I'm here! I'm here now. I'm sorry, dear.

749
00:53:32,919 --> 00:53:34,045
Uh…

750
00:53:34,128 --> 00:53:36,547
Ms. D, meet Professor Connie.

751
00:53:36,631 --> 00:53:38,090
Thank you for coming.

752
00:53:38,174 --> 00:53:40,843
-I'm sorry I'm late.
-It's all right.

753
00:53:40,927 --> 00:53:42,845
-It's a pleasure.
-Nice to meet you.

754
00:53:50,519 --> 00:53:52,063
At a very young age,

755
00:53:52,146 --> 00:53:53,981
I already knew what I really wanted to be,

756
00:53:54,065 --> 00:53:57,693
and that was to be
a successful businesswoman.

757
00:53:58,152 --> 00:53:59,654
To make my father proud.

758
00:54:01,238 --> 00:54:05,868
So when I was given
this huge responsibility…

759
00:54:07,119 --> 00:54:08,913
I didn't even flinch.

760
00:54:10,039 --> 00:54:13,125
I've sacrificed so much…

761
00:54:14,043 --> 00:54:16,462
to build and protect this business.

762
00:54:17,046 --> 00:54:19,799
Maybe that's why I'm called the Chairmom.

763
00:54:22,259 --> 00:54:24,387
If you were given a chance

764
00:54:24,470 --> 00:54:28,099
to choose between being
a CEO and being a mother,

765
00:54:28,975 --> 00:54:30,518
which one would you choose?

766
00:54:32,019 --> 00:54:34,355
I don't regret working hard

767
00:54:34,689 --> 00:54:37,441
because I'm not working hard
just for myself.

768
00:54:37,858 --> 00:54:42,113
It's for my family
and the people who depend on me.

769
00:54:42,655 --> 00:54:44,323
In a perfect world…

770
00:54:45,282 --> 00:54:49,161
You wouldn't have to choose
between having a career…

771
00:54:51,956 --> 00:54:53,791
and being a mother.

772
00:54:54,375 --> 00:54:56,544
You can be both. You can do both.

773
00:54:57,253 --> 00:55:01,799
And you should never have to apologize
for wanting to succeed.

774
00:55:01,882 --> 00:55:06,762
In business, I have solved
every little problem.

775
00:55:07,680 --> 00:55:11,183
Just like in business and motherhood…

776
00:55:12,268 --> 00:55:15,187
you're going to make a lot of mistakes.

777
00:55:20,776 --> 00:55:23,529
My father sent me to the most prestigious

778
00:55:23,612 --> 00:55:25,364
business schools.

779
00:55:25,448 --> 00:55:26,824
But, sadly…

780
00:55:28,451 --> 00:55:33,330
I wasn't given a manual
on how to be a good mother.

781
00:55:36,250 --> 00:55:37,460
And…

782
00:55:38,753 --> 00:55:40,504
there were times…

783
00:55:41,422 --> 00:55:45,551
that I struggled so much
trying to balance…

784
00:55:46,052 --> 00:55:49,972
being a good leader, a good wife, and…

785
00:55:51,265 --> 00:55:54,143
the kind of mother
that my daughter needed me to be.

786
00:55:56,353 --> 00:55:59,440
In a world that asks so much of you,

787
00:55:59,523 --> 00:56:01,859
do what gives you a purpose.

788
00:56:04,570 --> 00:56:05,905
You know, I realized…

789
00:56:07,073 --> 00:56:08,574
a bit late…

790
00:56:09,742 --> 00:56:10,868
that my loved ones…

791
00:56:11,285 --> 00:56:16,665
didn't always need me to fix everything
or to solve all their problems for them.

792
00:56:18,626 --> 00:56:22,421
Sometimes, all they needed
was for me to be there.

793
00:56:24,090 --> 00:56:27,968
To understand and to love them.

794
00:56:29,261 --> 00:56:31,597
With all your achievements,

795
00:56:32,431 --> 00:56:36,769
if you could give one piece of advice
to the younger generation,

796
00:56:37,478 --> 00:56:38,729
what would it be?

797
00:56:38,813 --> 00:56:40,106
So, my advice?

798
00:56:41,774 --> 00:56:44,610
Be whomever you want to be in this world.

799
00:56:45,736 --> 00:56:46,904
But…

800
00:56:47,446 --> 00:56:52,201
as you build the life you want to have,

801
00:56:52,493 --> 00:56:54,453
don't let go…

802
00:56:55,162 --> 00:56:59,625
of the things that make up who you are.

803
00:57:05,172 --> 00:57:08,259
We heard that your daughter
is studying here.

804
00:57:08,342 --> 00:57:10,010
Yes, yes. She's right there.

805
00:57:10,094 --> 00:57:13,973
Do you want to give her a message?

806
00:57:14,056 --> 00:57:17,768
Do you want her to grow up to be like you?

807
00:57:19,812 --> 00:57:22,690
I want her to be better than me.

808
00:57:25,151 --> 00:57:26,902
Much better.

809
00:57:28,070 --> 00:57:31,532
Actually, all I really want for her is…

810
00:57:31,615 --> 00:57:33,117
for her to be whole.

811
00:57:33,784 --> 00:57:35,578
For her to be happy.

812
00:57:37,079 --> 00:57:39,540
And I hope that…

813
00:57:40,583 --> 00:57:44,753
in all her wins or losses,

814
00:57:44,837 --> 00:57:48,799
I want her to know that
I'm just right here for her.

815
00:58:18,287 --> 00:58:20,706
-Thank you so much!
-Where's Patricia?

816
00:58:20,789 --> 00:58:22,208
-Thank you, ma'am.
-Thank you.

817
00:58:38,057 --> 00:58:39,141
Mom.

818
00:58:45,940 --> 00:58:47,441
You came.

819
00:59:31,860 --> 00:59:34,697
They're threatening you
because they're blaming you.

820
00:59:34,780 --> 00:59:37,491
I think this is a new enemy.

821
00:59:37,992 --> 00:59:40,703
What do you know
about the fire that happened back then?

822
00:59:40,786 --> 00:59:42,496
I will tell you once more.

823
00:59:42,579 --> 00:59:44,999
You don't have to go back
to what happened before.

824
00:59:45,082 --> 00:59:48,043
You have no memory
of what happened back then.

825
00:59:48,127 --> 00:59:49,753
We can correct what happened.

826
00:59:50,546 --> 00:59:51,964
You're often together.

827
00:59:52,047 --> 00:59:54,049
Is there something going on
between you and Mom?

828
00:59:54,133 --> 00:59:55,134
I like Diana.

829
00:59:55,217 --> 00:59:57,177
I want to be happy for Mom.

830
00:59:57,261 --> 00:59:58,387
But something feels wrong.
